===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*seh₁p-|*-os|*-s}}
From {{inh|en|enm|savour}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=sāvǒur|pos=n|id=MED38653}}</ref> from {{der|en|fro|savour}} (modern {{cog|fr|saveur}}), from {{der|en|la|sapor}},<ref>{{R:OED Online|entry=savour {{!}} savor|pos=n|id=5411002190|date=March 2024|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> . {{doublet|en|sapor}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}} {{term-label|en|British spelling}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} An [[aroma]] or [[smell#Noun|smell]].
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Edward 2|sig=&#91;I4&#93;|verso=1|page=73|passage=''Matr''[''euis'']. ''Gurney'', I vvonder the King dyes not, / Being in a Vault vp to the knees in vvater, / To vvhich the channels of the Baſtell runs, / {{...}} / ''Gur''[''ney'']. And ſo do I, ''Matreuis'': yeſternight / I opened but the doore to throvv him meate, / And I vvas almoſt ſtifled vvith the '''ſauour'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Georgics|book=4|lines=87–88|page=125|passage=Then Melfoil beat, and Honey-ſuckles pound, / VVith theſe alluring '''Savours''' ſtrevv the Ground; {{...}}|footer=Referring to the actions of bees.}}
#* {{RQ:Tatler|issue=148|date=21 March 1710|page=355|passage=[M]ethought I smelled the agreeable '''savour''' of roast beef; {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Falkner Moonfleet|year=1909|page=72|passage=He held out to me a bowl of steaming broth, that filled the room with a '''savour''' sweeter ten thousand times to me than every rose and lily of the world, yet would not let me drink it at a gulp, but made me sip it with a spoon like any baby.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[quality#Noun|quality]] which the [[sense#Noun|sense]] of [[taste#Noun|taste]] [[detect]]s; also {{lb|en|countable}}, a [[specific]] [[flavor#Noun|flavour]] or taste, especially one [[different#Adjective|different]] from the [[predominant#Adjective|predominant]] one.
##* {{RQ:De Mornay Sidney Golding Trewnesse|chapter=That there is a God, and that All Men Agree in the Godhead|page=7|passage=[B]y our Sences which conceiue al Colours, Sounds, Sents, '''Sauors''', and Féelings; wee may ſee, heare, ſmell, taſt, and feele, that one ſelfſame workman made both the Sences, and the things that are ſubiect to the Sences.}}
##* {{RQ:Vance Nobody|chapter=Anarchy|pages=18–19|pageref=19|passage=Little disappointed, then, she turned attention to "Chat of the Social World," gossip which exercised potent fascination upon the girl's intelligence. She devoured with more avidity than she had her food those pretentiously phrased chronicles of the snobocracy— {{...}} distilling therefrom an acid envy that robbed her napoleon {{quote-gloss|a millefeuille pastry}} of all its '''savour'''.}}
## {{lb|en|countable|chiefly in the negative}} An [[appealing#Adjective|appealing]] or [[appetizing#Adjective|appetizing]] flavour, especially one which is [[savory#Adjective|savoury]] or [[strong#Adjective|strong]].
# {{lb|en|figurative}}
## {{lb|en|countable}} A [[distinctive#Adjective|distinctive]] [[sensation]] like a flavour or taste, or an aroma or smell.
##* {{RQ:Baxter Saints|chapter=What Affections Must be Acted, and by what Considerations and Obje[c]ts, and in what Order|section=IX|para=5|page=747|passage=[W]hy is not my life a continual Joy? and the '''ſavor''' of Heaven perpetually upon my ſpirit?}}
## {{lb|en|countable}} A [[particular#Adjective|particular]] quality, especially a [[small#Adjective|small]] [[amount#Noun|amount]] of it; a [[hint#Noun|hint]] or [[trace#Noun|trace]] of something.
##: {{synonyms|en|tinge}}
## {{lb|en|countable|chiefly in the negative}} A quality which is appealing or [[enjoyable]]; [[merit#Noun|merit]], [[value#Noun|value]].
## {{lb|en|countable|archaic}} A [[reputation]].
##* {{RQ:Coverdale Bible|Exodus|5|19|folio=xxv|verso=1|column=2|passage=The LORDE loke vpon you, & iudge it, for ye haue made the '''ſauoure''' of vs to ſtynke before Pharao and his ſeruauntes, and haue geuen them a ſwerde in their handes, to ſlaye vs.}}
##* {{RQ:Fuller Holy Warre|chapter=The Ecclesiasticall Affairs in this Kings Reigne|page=64|passage=VVe left Arnulphus {{quote-gloss|''i.e.'', {{w|Arnulf of Chocques}}}} the laſt Patriarch of Jeruſalem; ſince vvhich time the bad '''ſavour''' of his life came to the Popes noſe, vvho ſent a Legate to depoſe him.}}
##* {{RQ:Tennyson Idylls|edition=cabinet|volume=V|poem=Gareth and Lynette|page=52|passage=Then came in hall the messenger of Mark, / A name of evil '''savour''' in the land, / The Cornish king.}}
## {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[enjoyment|Enjoyment]] or taste for something; [[appreciation]]; [[pleasure#Noun|pleasure]]; [[relish#Noun|relish]]; {{lb|en|countable}} an [[instance#Noun|instance]] of this.
## {{lb|en|uncountable|obsolete}} [[knowledge#Noun|Knowledge]]; [[understanding#Noun|understanding]].
##* {{RQ:Herbert Temple|chapter=Dialogue|page=107|passage=But as I can ſee no merit; / Leading to this favour: / So the vvay to fit me for it, / Is beyond my '''ſavour'''.}}

